 Best architecture for smooth demo
Demo sequence (everything automatic):

1. User types "a stunning forest" in Electron app
2. User clicks Generate in Electron
3. Electron → POST /api/generate/image (with X-License-Key)
4. Backend creates BullMQ job → responds 202 immediately
5. Electron shows loading skeleton
6. Worker picks up job → calls flowProxy.generateImage()
7. flowProxy:
   a. Opens off-screen Chrome (invisible)
   b. Creates Flow project (via fetch in page context)
   c. Navigates to project page
   d. Waits for networkidle (React fully mounted)
   e. Types prompt (with real keyboard events)
   f. Clicks Generate (with hover + scroll into view)
   g. Intercepts batchGenerateImages response
   h. Extracts fifeUrl
8. Job marked completed with output_url
9. Electron polls every 3s → gets completed + URL
10. Image renders in Electron app
11. Chrome page closes (genPage.close())

Total time: 30–45 seconds
User sees: loading animation → image
User never sees: Chrome, Flow, Google, API calls

